// Title: Remote Access Tool - RURAT Execution From Unusual Location
// Sigma ID: e01fa958-6893-41d4-ae03-182477c5e77d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-19 | Modified: 2023-03-05
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects execution of Remote Utilities RAT (RURAT) from an unusual location (outside of
//   'C:\Program Files')
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/misbehaving-rats/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_remote_access_tools_rurat_non_default_location.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\rutserv.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\rfusclient.exe") or ProcessVersionInfoProductName =~ "Remote Utilities") and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Remote Utilities" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Remote Utilities")))
